{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration and obstacle-recovery policy in specifications. The policy gives one controllable action per decision/recovery state, keeps all uncontrollable events defined in every specification state, treats obstacle events as safety-critical preemptions in action states, uses brief directed turns as default recovery, reserves move_backward only for front-obstacle escape, and reserves full_rotate only for a dedicated repeated-failure last-resort path.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensor outcomes from motion capabilities in plant automata so specifications can bind perception to safe actions.",
    "Use one-shot action/commit states in the specifications so open-loop pulses execute once, with obstacle events able to preempt and path_clear usually self-looping in action states.",
    "Bias toward coverage by making clear-space exploration default to move_forward, using random_walk only after a last-resort scan to break deadlock, and returning to forward progress immediately when path_clear appears."
  ],
  "G": [
    {
      "name": "G1",
      "purpose": "Perception channel for obstacle and clear-path sensor outcomes",
      "states": [
        "sense"
      ],
      "initial_states": [
        "sense"
      ],
      "marked_states": [
        "sense"
      ],
      "controllable_events": [],
